{"slug":"falling-trendline-breakout","name":"Falling trendline breakout","status":"rejected","created_at":"2026-11-05T03:28:30.567298Z","version":1,"frozen":true,"implementation":"trendline-breakout","runs":2,"trials":2,"deflated_sharpe":2.993742143075906e-08,"asset_class":"crypto","sections":{"hypothesis":"Hypothesis","rationale":"Why the edge should exist","rules":"Rules in plain English","falsification":"What would prove it wrong","parameters":"Parameters and allowed ranges","costs":"Expected turnover against costs"},"notes":[{"version":1,"created_at":"2026-11-05T03:28:30.567298Z","sections":{"hypothesis":"When price closes decisively above a falling trendline drawn through the two most recent known lower swing highs, the breakout reaches 3R more often than its cost-adjusted break-even rate (about 26%).","rationale":"The breakout marks the end of a sequence of lower highs: sellers stop pressing, and momentum and stop-buying from shorts may follow. It is the trendline version of a plain breakout, so the real question is whether the line adds anything over a horizontal channel high. Weak point: many breaks of a falling line are just pauses in the down-trend.","rules":"Shared definitions: 4h bars; swing high/low = a bar's high (low) beats the 3 bars before it and isn't beaten by the 3 bars after it, known only 3 bars later; ATR = 14-bar average true range at the signal bar. Lines and levels use only swings known at the signal bar. Buy at the next open; risk 1% per trade (spot, no leverage); one position at a time. Line: through the two most recent known swing highs, where the later one is lower, projected forward. Breakout: a close more than 0.5 ATR above the projected line. That close is the signal. Stop: the lowest low since the later swing high. Target: 3R. One entry per line.","falsification":"BTCUSDT and ETHUSDT 4h, 2020-01 to 2025-10 (before the holdout), default parameters, run once. Reject if, pooled across both markets: net expectancy after costs is 0R or below; or P(expectancy > 0) is under 90%; or fewer than 50 trades; or it doesn't beat the channel-breakout engine test with a 3R target and 1% risk on the same data (a horizontal 20-bar high instead of a falling line).","parameters":"swing_bars 3 (2-5); breakout_atr_pct 50 (25-100); target_r 3 (2-4). Comparison: channel-breakout with lookback 20, stop_lookback 10, target_r 3. Only the defaults are pre-registered.","costs":"The stop sits at a recent low, which can be far below a breakout close: often 5-10% on 4h, so costs are small, about 0.02-0.05R. Wide stops also mean smaller positions and some trades capped by cash. Expect 1-3 setups a month per market."},"implementation":"trendline-breakout","frozen_at":"2026-11-11T13:05:25.568600Z","change_reason":null}],"history":[{"status":"idea","at":"2026-11-05T03:28:30.567298Z","reason":"Created"},{"status":"specified","at":"2026-11-11T13:05:25.568637Z","reason":"v1 frozen"},{"status":"backtested","at":"2026-11-11T13:05:30.590128Z","reason":"first run on v1"},{"status":"rejected","at":"2026-11-14T08:43:25.507852Z","reason":"Tested 2026-11-05 on BTC and ETH 4h: lost money on average, while its control (a plain breakout of the recent high) made money. Recorded as drop; closed in the 2026-11-14 clean-out."}],"trial_log":[{"id":"20261111-130530-0164ca","created_at":"2026-11-11T13:05:30.581025Z","strategy":"trendline-breakout","strategy_kind":"research","style":"brackets","engine":"event","params":{"swing_bars":3,"breakout_atr_pct":50,"target_r":3},"research":{"slug":"falling-trendline-breakout","version":1},"strategy_name":"falling trendline breakout 3R BTCUSDT","symbol":"BTCUSDT","benchmark_symbol":null,"universe_coins":null,"forced_exits":0,"deflated_sharpe":8.122679751032535e-10,"deflated_trials":883,"interval":"4h","start":"2020-01","end":"2025-10","scored_from":null,"history_from":null,"initial_cash":"330.0","account_currency":"USDT","used_holdout":false,"config_fingerprint":"058563faed8a","code":{"commit":"4a85c28b7724064